2025-09-16 21:04:08,803 INFO: {'cv_text_summary': '[0]Summary: Marcos David Madrigal Albores, Computer Engineer, can be contacted at 308 Brunswick Ave, +1-437-981-2994, marcosdma.compeng@outlook.com, linkedin.com/in/marcosdma/, and github.com/marneus981. With a Minor in Artificial Intelligence from the University of Toronto (2023), Marcos is certified in AI principles and applications. He holds a Bachelor of Applied Science in Computer Engineering from the University of Toronto (2018/09 - 2023/06) with coursework including computer algorithms, electric circuits, calculus, programming fundamentals, and linear algebra.', 'cv_text': "[0]Name: Marcos David Madrigal Albores\n[0]Contact Information:\n[1]Address: 308 Brunswick Ave, Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Phone: +1-437-981-2994\n[1]Email: marcosdma.compeng@outlook.com\n[1]LinkedIn: linkedin.com/in/marcosdma/\n[1]Github: github.com/marneus981\n[1]Portfolio: marneus981.github.io | donkeyponius981.itch.io\n[0]Title: Computer Engineer\n[0]Summary: As a detail-oriented and adaptable individual, I leverage my proficiency in Python and JavaScript to drive innovative software solutions. With practical experience gained through previous internships, I excel in algorithmic thinking, version control, and unit testing. Now, I'm eager to join Sentry as a Software Engineer, New Grad, where I can collaborate with a team, learn from feedback, and contribute to the development of the Sentry product.\n[0]Languages: English, Spanish, French\n[0]Education:\n[1]Degree: Bachelor of Applied Science in Computer Engineering\n[1]University: University of Toronto\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2018/09 - 2023/06\n[1]Courses: [1]Courses: ESC190 Computer Algorithms and Data Structures, ECE159 Fundamentals of Electric Circuits, MAT195 Calculus II, ECE244 Programming Fundamentals, MAT185 Linear Algebra\n[0]Certifications:\n[1]Certification Name: Minor in Artificial Intelligence\n[1]Issuing Organization: University of Toronto\n[1]Issue Date: 2023/06\n[0]Awards and Scholarships:\n[1]Award Name: United Nations Datathon 2023 Participation\n[1]Issuing Organization: United Nations\n[1]Issue Date: 2023/11\n[1]Award Name: University of Toronto Engineering Scholar\n[1]Issuing Organization: University of Toronto Faculty of Applied Science and Engineering\n[1]Issue Date: 2018/09\n[0]Volunteering and Leadership:\n[1]Role: Engineering Science Program Ambassador\n[1]Organization: Engineering Science Department Ambassador Program, University of Toronto\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2019/01 - 2019/06\n[1]Description: Represented the Engineering Science Department at Student Outreach and Department-Organized Summits and Conferences, honing communication skills and adaptability\n[0]Work Experience:\n[1]Job Title: Script Programmer and Video Project Editor\n[1]Company: Ontario Institute for Studies in Education\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2022/03 - 2022/05\n[1]Description: Developed video description generation algorithms using Python ML, collaborating with stakeholders to ensure project deliverables met expectations. Highlighted effective communication and collaboration skills in a fast-paced project environment\n[0]Projects:\n[1]Project Title: Horizontal Federated Learning Research\n[1]URL: github.com/alexjsenn/FedScale\n[1]Type: Research | Capstone Project\n[1]Duration: 2021/09 - 2022/06\n[1]Description: Researched and developed a Federated Machine Learning model aggregation algorithm, doubling network efficiency with comparable model performance. Co-authored technical papers and presentations on novel aggregation algorithms\n[1]Project Title: Neural Signal Modelling\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/NeuralBioelectricityProject\n[1]Type: University Project\n[1]Duration: 2020/09 - 2020/12\n[1]Description: Researched neural signal transmission and propagation, leveraging MATLAB to simulate complex systems. Applied analytical problem-solving skills to develop a holistic simulation\n[1]Project Title: MAPPA C++ Geographical Information System\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/MAPPA\n[1]Type: University Project\n[1]Duration: 2019/09 - 2020/06\n[1]Description: Built a GIS system using OpenStreetMap data and C++ EZGL Library. Improved efficiency by 200% and reduced memory usage by 50%, showcasing algorithmic thinking and software development skills\n[0]Skills:\n[1]Programming Languages: Python, JavaScript, Scripting\n[1]Technical Skills: Algorithm Optimization, Data Analysis, Machine Learning, OpenStreetMap API, Unit Testing\n[1]Soft Skills: Effective Communication, Adaptability, Collaboration, Good Written and Communication Skills", 'job_description': "Company Name: Sentry  \nJob Title: Software Engineer - New Grad\n\n### Key Responsibilities:\n- Collaborate on developing and enhancing Sentry's software products using Python or JavaScript.\n- Engage in the full software development lifecycle, including design, implementation, testing, and production operations.\n- Foster communication with team members, other departments, and stakeholders like product managers.\n\n### Requirements & Skills:\n\n#### Technical Skills:\n- Possess a B.S. or higher in Computer Science or a related field.\n- Minimum of 1 previous internship or equivalent practical experience in software development.\n- Proficiency in one or more general-purpose programming languages such as Python, JavaScript, Java, etc.\n- Solid understanding of algorithms, data structures, and object-oriented design principles.\n\n#### Soft Skills:\n- Demonstrate the ability to effectively communicate with team members and various stakeholders.\n- Actively seek feedback for improvement from managers and peers.\n- Show enthusiasm for using the product you're building daily (we dogfood Sentry every day).\n- Exhibit a willingness to join a dynamic, fast-paced startup culture that values continuous learning.\n\n### Highlighted Skills:\n- Full software development lifecycle proficiency\n- Strong technical foundation in programming languages and software design principles\n- Effective communication within teams and with stakeholders", 'standard_calls': ['make_cover_letter_text'], 'non_standard_calls': []}
